{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gts360/django-mcp-server/pulls/72","id":4513887432,"node_id":"PR_kwDOOns7hc8AAAABDQx0yA","html_url":"https://github.com/gts360/django-mcp-server/pull/72","diff_url":"https://github.com/gts360/django-mcp-server/pull/72.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/gts360/django-mcp-server/pull/72.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gts360/django-mcp-server/issues/72","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gts360/django-mcp-server/pulls/72/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gts360/django-mcp-server/pulls/72/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gts360/django-mcp-server/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gts360/django-mcp-server/issues/72/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gts360/django-mcp-server/statuses/800c16d4815c9ed80bf0481268b45e879162d599","number":72,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"security: validate $match/$project field paths against allowed_models/exclude_fields","user":{"login":"kemrec","id":25618690,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1NjE4Njkw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/25618690?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kemrec","html_url":"https://github.com/kemrec","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kemrec/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kemrec/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kemrec/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kemrec/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kemrec/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kemrec/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kemrec/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kemrec/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kemrec/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What this fixes\n\n`_parse_match()` and `_interpret_projection()` built their field paths straight from caller input and passed them to `Q()`/`.values()` with no check against `get_published_models()` or `get_excluded_fields()`. Those two allowlists were only ever consulted for `$lookup` and for building the schema advertised to the calling model — never at query execution time.\n\nSince the whole left-hand side of a `$match` key is caller-controlled, this also lets a Django lookup/transform be smuggled in via the field name itself (e.g. `author__password__startswith`), bypassing the `$`-operator allowlist a few lines above it.\n\n**Net effect:** an MCP client that can query one published model can traverse any FK/M2M/reverse relation from it — including into models that were never registered with a `ModelQueryToolset` at all — and use equality/`startswith`/`regex` filters as a character-level read oracle over any field it finds, including fields explicitly listed in `exclude_fields`. Publishing a single model whose rows relate (even transitively) to `auth.User` is enough to read out password hashes one character at a time.\n\nI reported this privately by email first; this PR accompanies that report and I'm happy to also file it as a GitHub Security Advisory once private vulnerability reporting is enabled on this repo.\n\n## The fix\n\n- Adds `_validate_field_path()`, mirroring the existing `_validate_lookup()`/`_resolve_model_from_path()` logic already used for `$lookup`: walk the `__`-separated path hop by hop, require each hop to be a real field, refuse a relation hop into an unpublished model, and refuse any hop that is an excluded field.\n- Threaded through `_parse_match` (including its `$and`/`$or`/`$nor` recursion) and `_interpret_projection` — `$project` turned out to have the identical gap, not just `$match`.\n- The no-`$project` default output path now builds its field list from the model's concrete fields minus `excluded_fields`, so `exclude_fields` actually keeps a field out of the *response*, not only out of the schema shown to the model.\n\n## Verification\n\nTested against a PoC (one published `Article` model, `exclude_fields=[\"internal_note\"]`, `auth.User` never published):\n\n- Intended query (`{\"title\": \"Public post\"}`) is unaffected, and now correctly omits `internal_note`/`author_id` from the response body too (previously present despite `exclude_fields`).\n- `{\"internal_note\": {\"$regex\": \"...\"}}` → `Invalid field path 'internal_note': field 'internal_note' is not available.`\n- `{\"author__password__startswith\": \"pbkdf2_sha256\"}` → `Invalid field path '...': field 'author' is not available.`\n- Full traversal matrix (m2m, reverse relations, unrelated apps via `auth.User`, `$regex`/`$year__gt` operators) uniformly rejected.\n- `$project` on an excluded/unpublished-model field rejected the same way.\n- No existing behavior for allowed fields/models changed.\n\n## Left as suggestions, not part of this diff\n\n- `$regex` stays available for any field that *is* published — this PR only restricts which fields/models are reachable, not lookup selection. If you'd also like to restrict `$regex` specifically (it's an efficient character-oracle and a mild ReDoS vector even on a published field), that's a separate, smaller change worth its own discussion.\n- Unrelated: `pyproject.toml` pins `mcp (>=1.8.0)` with no upper bound, but current imports don't resolve against `mcp` 2.x on a fresh install — worth a version pin whenever convenient.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-09-12T15:06:54Z","updated_at":"2026-11-07T18:26:01Z","closed_at":"2026-11-07T18:26:01Z","merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"760c65fe65fa4406a278bc196eed659c2f22902f","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"kemrec:fix/mcp-match-project-field-path-validation","ref":"fix/mcp-match-project-field-path-validation","repo":null,"sha":"800c16d4815c9ed80bf0481268b45e879162d599","user":{"login":"kemrec","id":25618690,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1NjE4Njkw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/25618690?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kemrec","html_url":"https://github.com/kemrec","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kemrec/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kemrec/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kemrec/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kemrec/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kemrec/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kemrec/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kemrec/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kemrec/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kemrec/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},"base":{"label":"gts360:main","ref":"main","repo":{"id":981154693,"node_id":"R_kgDOOns7hQ","name":"django-mcp-server","full_name":"gts360/django-mcp-server","owner":{"login":"gts360","id":240693943,"node_id":"O_kgDODliytw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/240693943?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gts360","html_url":"https://github.com/gts360","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gts360/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gts360/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gts360/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gts360/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gts360/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gts360/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gts360/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gts360/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gts360/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"p